@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
title Plant devices at the runtime HMI (specification 39, §21.2, §21.4, §21.5)
actor "Named operator / engineer" as Operator
component "HMI HTTP service\nSession, role, origin check" as Web
component "Method command\nInterface, method, instance, permit, inputs" as Command
component "Settings route\nRead / apply with expected values (Engineer)" as Settings
queue "Bounded queue\nPer-user replay records" as Queue
component "Hmi.Display boundary\nBetween scans" as Boundary
component "VM method call / RETAIN member write" as VM
component "Plant device instance\nMode decides who commands" as FB
component "Audit and outcome streams" as Audit
component "IEC retain service\nInstance member paths" as Store
component "Runtime alarm board\nEvery Alarm instance once, where it is declared\n(interface and reference members not followed)" as Alarms
Operator --> Web
Web --> Command : command in Manual
Web --> Settings : Engineer only
Command --> Queue : interlock permit checked first
Settings --> Queue : all changes at one boundary
Boundary --> Queue : bounded drain; never waits for HTTP
Boundary --> VM
VM --> FB
FB --> Web : BOOL outcome; CommandText as the reason;\nReasonText as the panel's message line
Web --> Audit
FB ..> Store : public RETAIN settings, counters, mode
FB --> Alarms : alarm members (P101.TripAlarm)
Alarms --> Web
note bottom of Boundary
A pulse always ends, even after a disconnect. No request number,
owner or context reaches PLC code. Ordinary I/O and the task schedule
stay in place.
end note
@enduml
